  "term": "Carpenter’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Carpenter’s syndrome is an extremely rare inherited disorder marked by early joining of the skull bones, a cone-shaped head, and abnormalities of the fingers or toes such as fusion or extra digits. It can also occur with heart or kidney defects, short stature, undescended testes, and mild intellectual impairment.",
